&lt;h3&gt;


  12) Metrics to track
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pass rate per page and per route (0 violations, 1-2 minor, 3+ critical).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Number of new violations introduced per PR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time to fix accessibility issues (from report to merged fix).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contrast ratio compliance percentage across tokens and components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Screen reader validation pass rate for critical flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


  13) Common pitfalls and how to avoid them
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Treating a11y as a checkbox rather than a continuous improvement process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution: Integrate it into design-review, code-review, and release gates with clear owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Over-optimizing for automated checks at the expense of real user experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution: Use manual testing as a supplement to automated tests; automated checks catch many issues, but human validation catches nuance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ARIA overuse or misuse.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution: Favor native semantics; use ARIA only when necessary to convey information not available with native elements.
### 14) Example outcome and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;/li&gt;

